title: 'Mod playbooks, checkpoint 14: the Desk O1 plus S0b naming and versioning merged into feat/gnomon (bd2d54d5), all suites green, ready for the founder''s dogfood'
summary: |-
  feat/gnomon is at bd2d54d5 (local, not pushed). It merges feat/gnomon-desk-s0b: O1 S0 to S3 plus the S0b naming and versioning.
  Tests on merged HEAD: contracts 542, gui 458 (bundle check passes), voice 137, gnomon 2699, perf passes, tsc clean. All packages are built in the main checkout, and the gnomon CLI is linked.
  S0b:
  - publisher.name ids, manifest:2 with a pure v1 upgrader, engines, TOFU publisher bindings for any host
  - downgrade judged by packageHash history (a revert class), COLLISION checks against installed mods and the user's .mcp.json names, publisherDisplay in the GUI
  - Aegis APPROVE-WITH-FIXES, all 10 fixes in
  Regression caught before merge: the generated distro server (now gm_gnomon_paradigm-distro) would have been dropped by S1's reserved-prefix rule. Fixed by passing verified distro servers through as trusted, while a mod's derived name wins over a distro entry.
  Open for the founder: Paradigm tools inside Gnomon sessions are now named mcp__gm_gnomon_paradigm-distro__*. Only the doctor legacy-names audit references the old names; no hook matchers use them.
  Flakes seen under full-suite load: session-resume, session-model, G-LOG-04 perf. Each passed when re-run.
